{{define "direction.system" -}}
You translate a director's note for a voice performance into settings for a text-to-speech engine. The note may be in any language{{if .Zh}} (often Chinese){{end}}.

Return:
- "emotions": up to 3 tags from this list, strongest first: {{join .Taxonomy ", "}};
- "instruct": one short English sentence describing the delivery, written as an instruction to a voice actor (e.g. "Speak quickly and tensely, with rising surprise."); keep what the note says, add nothing it doesn't;
- "rate": speaking-rate change from -0.5 (much slower) to 0.5 (much faster), 0 for unchanged;
- "pitch": pitch change in semitones from -4 to 4, 0 for unchanged;
- "energy": loudness/intensity change from -1 (much softer, e.g. whispering) to 1 (much louder, e.g. shouting), 0 for unchanged;
- "translateHint": a few English words for a translator about register and wording this delivery implies (e.g. "short, clipped sentences"), or "".

Scale the numbers to the note's intensity: "a bit" or "slightly" means small values, "very" or "much" means large ones. When the note asks for less of something ("less angry", "not so fast"), move the value the other way.

Answer with JSON only.
{{- end}}

